 Equating this to 7/51 gives 7k²-102k-160 = (k-16)(7k+10) = 0. The only valid integer base greater than 3 is 16.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_024"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2019_AMC_12A_Q11","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"shift-repeating-block","label":"Shift the repeating block","methodDirectNodeIds":{"shift-repeating-block":["cnm_024","cnm_224"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_024","cnm_224"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":1,"alignmentIds":["alignment:a987b535779e9a21d69ef6f7"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"E: b = 8","reason":"The difference is 2b³ + 2b + 1 - (2b² + 2b + 1) = 2b²(b - 1). It is divisible by 3 when b is congruent to 0 or 1 modulo 3, but not when b is congruent to 2. Only 8 has the latter residue.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_024"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2021_AMC_10A_Q11","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"primary","label":"Expand base notation and factor for divisibility.","methodDirectNodeIds":{"primary":["cnm_024","math:modular-congruence"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_024","math:modular-congruence"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":1,"alignmentIds":["alignment:a987b535779e9a21d69ef6f7"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B, 11","reason":"The expansions give 3n^2+2n+d=263 and 3n^2+2n+4=253+6d. Substitution yields 267-d=253+6d, so d=2. Then (n-9)(3n+29)=0; the positive base is n=9, giving n+d=11.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_024"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2021_AMC_10B_Q13","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"eliminate-shared-place-values","label":"Eliminate the shared place values","methodDirectNodeIds":{"eliminate-shared-place-values":["cnm_024","cnm_042","cnm_224"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_024","cnm_042","cnm_224"]},{"contextN